your logging.properties file is fine if you you are using statically assigned logging levels that dont change during your application's 
runtime.

However if you wish to turn on/off logging at runtime use jvisualvm (this tool is really kickass) goto MBeans->java.util.logging->
->Click on Operations

getLoggerLevel type in the full class name w/o any quotation marks around it and hit enter 

likewise for the getParentLoggerName

to change the logger level use setLoggerLevel ( fullClassName, Level in string )

for example
setLoggerLevel org.kbanerjee.local.sortedsetallocators.SortedSetAllocator  INFO ( or OFF ) will do the trick.

when the methods are invoked successfully it will prompt you with a dialog box saying method invocation was successful.

NOTE:
You might want to keep this MBeans concept in mind so you could write your own component MBeans to control at runtime.